                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "really fun spin on tetris. place falling shapes and create chains with matching colors (diagonals work too), then detonate them with a glowing detonator block or link different colors with a coupler for an even bigger effect. a chain of at least 7 grants an item (destroy half of a color or the bottom row, etc.). [b]local multiplayer[/b] is also available with more items and stuff. the how to play section explains all this, but if you skip the offered tutorial on first startup like I did (to adjust blaring audio first), you won't get another chance. then again, it might just be the same screens.\n\nmultiplayer is customizable (items on/off, start level, p1/p2 handicap) and there are [b]4 single player game modes[/b]. endless is endless, mission has a series of objectives to complete, time attack has a time limit, race has a certain amount of points to reach. they can be played with or without items and a starting level can be chosen as well, plus 2, 4 or 6 minutes for time attack and 50k, 100k or 250k points for race mode.\n\n[b]rebindable controls[/b] is good news because backspace for 'fast down' and rotate in reverse with right shift is crazy. too bad space can't be bound. other settings are separate volumes, camera shake toggle, resolutions (not in a pull-down menu, gotta click through them one by one), windowed mode, overall detail setting (low/high only), anti-aliasing, v-sync, vibration. [b]no colorblind option[/b] but there's a stats and in-game achievements screen, plus local and online leaderboards for each mode, with or without items. all of these are available anytime and [b]the game is fully keyboardable[/b] but obviously not mousable outside the menus.\n\nit's tetris but different enough and can entertain for a while or longer, depending on how good you wanna get at it. I saw tens of millions of points (assuming they're legit), no thank you, I was lucky to get a few million a few times. 14 million just once but it it was in mission mode where it doesn't count. still, [b]I enjoyed it a great deal[/b], not bad for 4 eur. music is good too, except for the incredibly repetitive short loop in the main menu. I would've liked hotkeys to select items instead of always using the latest one, but no complaints otherwise.",
